-- FIX-1 (end-of-sprint review S0-1, the INFERRED twin): the same
-- multi-parameter structured predicate with NO signature at all.
--
-- 🚨 THIS ROW IS NOT ITS SIBLING'S CONTROL -- IT TAKES A DIFFERENT CHANNEL AND
-- WAS FIXED BY A DIFFERENT CONJUNCT.  `s-multiparam-structured-declared-
-- rejected.mdk` is caught because `h`'s declared context is already REGISTERED
-- when the body goal is checked, so the goal is "claimed" and must match a
-- given.  Here nothing is registered at all: `inferredConstraintIds` rejects the
-- compound `Wrap t`, `ids` comes out empty, and `registerInferredFor` returns on
-- its empty-ids guard -- so the goal is UNCLAIMED and the claimed-test alone
-- lets it through.  What refuses it is `goalSlotStillOpen`'s ARITY half: a
-- 2-ary vector can never acquire a given on ANY channel, because
-- `registerPredGiven` matches `[subject]` and is the only writer that answers a
-- structured goal.  MEASURED: with the claimed-test alone this file printed
-- `boolInt/boolInt` at exit 0 while its declared sibling already rejected --
-- i.e. OD6(a)'s declared/inferred agreement held only by disagreeing.
--
-- Correct answer, hand-derived from §3: `h True` grounds to
-- `Conv (Wrap Bool) Int` and `h 1` to `Conv (Wrap Int) Int`, so a tree that
-- could dispatch this would print `boolInt/intInt`.  It cannot, so REJECT.
--
-- At the pre-fix sprint head `aa36d555`: check 0, run 0 and build 0, all
-- printing `boolInt/boolInt` -- the first impl's body for both calls.
--
-- ⚠️ VERDICT AND CODE, NO LOCATION.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

interface Conv s t where
  conv : s -> t -> String

impl Conv (Wrap Bool) Int where
  conv _ _ = "boolInt"

impl Conv (Wrap Int) Int where
  conv _ _ = "intInt"

h x = conv (Wrap x) 0

main = println "\{h True}/\{h 1}"
